  "issue_number": 18,
  "issue_title": "Webhook endpoints skip auth when secret is unset/default (\"replace-me\")",
  "issue_body": "## Title\nwebhook auth is effectively disabled when `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset/default (`replace-me`)\n\n## Summary\n\nWebhook verification currently short-circuits when the configured secret is empty or left at the default `replace-me`.\n\nIn `validator/src/eval_backend/api/routes.py`:\n\n- `_verify_github_signature(...)` returns early if `not secret or secret == \"replace-me\"`\n- `_verify_shared_secret(...)` does the same\n\nThis means a misconfigured deployment can accept unsigned/unauthenticated webhook requests.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis is a security and integrity risk for submission intake:\n\n- `/webhooks/github` may accept forged GitHub webhook payloads\n- `/webhooks/github/submission` may accept forged submission uploads\n- unauthorized actors could enqueue bogus evaluations or manipulate workflow state\n\nBecause `replace-me` is also the default in config, this failure mode is easy to hit in real environments.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nMake webhook auth fail-closed by default:\n\n1. Treat missing/default secret as configuration error for webhook routes (HTTP 500 or explicit startup-time validation).\n2. Never bypass signature/secret checks on webhook endpoints.\n3. Add clear logs/errors instructing operators to set `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`.\n4. Optionally gate dev-only bypass behind an explicit opt-in env var (e.g. `ALLOW_INSECURE_WEBHOOKS=1`) and default it to off.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Webhook endpoints do **not** accept requests when secret is unset/default\n- Invalid/missing signature/secret returns 401\n- Valid signature/secret still passes\n- Tests cover:\n  - default secret -> fail-closed behavior\n  - invalid signature/secret -> 401\n  - valid signature/secret -> success",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-08T20:05:04.000Z",
